ge of I guess the range  of research is almost as broad as the  number the huge number of applications  for this particular product so while  we're in the AG department we often  think about agronomic research I mean it  goes from agronomic research to you know  setting cultivars growing conditions but  it also involves market research and  production so it's an entire array of  possibilities some of which we are quite  familiar with and some of which we  haven't traditionally been involved in  so it's a learning process on our part  one of the fun things about listening to  all these panelists is a lot of it you  sort of going yeah I learned that but  there's so much more to learn so from  the legal side it's a really exciting  area because it both exposes your  knowledge base and also your profound  ignorance without what can happen so  it's sort of like a lot of fun because  one a lot of the things we see and that  the department has done has been done  over time and it's a building effort and  we're dealing with structures that  already been created this is a new  opportunity it's a new program so you  can form it and mold it and try to make  it work as efficiently as possible which  is both challenging and is an exciting  so it's interesting for me hopefully  it's interesting and useful for you and  I can't emphasize how important it is to  get input from the folks who are there  in the fields doing the research doing  the growing and getting information  because I mean regulations just really  rules of the game so we try to create  certainty and clarity everyone knows  what's going on and you can perform in a  relatively easy environment they cost  what's required is clear and it's it  addresses sort of your needs so saying  all of that i'll give you a breezy intro  duction to what our program currently  looks like and essentially will look  like because it's really it's pretty  simple notwithstanding and the  challenges we're working in a murky  federal envir